          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "In Sydney’s prestige property market (typically $5 million to $50 million-plus), a substantial share of transactions occur **off-market** or pre-market. In this segment, the role of a buyer’s advocate extends beyond finding listings to unlocking discreet opportunities, providing objective valuation, ensuring privacy, and navigating high-stakes negotiations.\n\nThe leading luxury buyers agencies and advocates in Sydney known for their pedigree, access, and acquisition advisory in the prestige space include:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Boutique Prestige Specialists & Dealmakers\n\n* **SydneySlice (Deborah West & Stephen Smith)**\n  * **Core Areas:** Eastern Suburbs, Lower North Shore, Harbourside estates.\n  * **Reputation:** Established in 2000, SydneySlice is one of the most respected boutique advisory firms in the ultra-high-net-worth (UHNW) and expat space. They maintain a low profile and focus heavily on private, highly tailored acquisitions. They are particularly well known for securing prime harbourside residences and large family estates off-market.\n  * **Best For:** Ultra-high-net-worth families, expats, and downsizers requiring discretion and deep local integration.\n\n* **Goldman Bros (Barry Goldman & Mark Goldman)**\n  * **Core Areas:** Eastern Suburbs (Vaucluse, Bellevue Hill, Point Piper, Double Bay, Rose Bay).\n  * **Reputation:** Transitioning from years as senior luxury sales agents at Sydney Sotheby’s International Realty, the Goldman brothers exclusively represent buyers in the $5M to $50M+ range. Because they spent decades operating on the sales side of Sydney's most expensive real estate, they possess direct access to trophy homeowners and selling agents.\n  * **Best For:** Buyers seeking top-tier Eastern Suburbs trophy homes and waterfront estates.\n\n* **Rose & Jones (Byron Rose & Stuart Jones)**\n  * **Core Areas:** Eastern Suburbs, Inner East, Lower North Shore.\n  * **Reputation:** Founded in 1998, Rose & Jones is one of Sydney’s oldest and most institutional buyers agencies. They are known for a measured, research-backed methodology that blends acquisition advocacy with long-term capital preservation. They represent prominent Australian families, trusts, and commercial investors.\n  * **Best For:** Methodical buyers who place high value on analytical due diligence and structured advisory.\n\n---\n\n### 2. High-Volume & High-Reach Networks\n\n* **Cohen Handler (Simon Cohen)**\n  * **Core Areas:** Eastern Suburbs, Lower North Shore, Northern Beaches.\n  * **Reputation:** Australia’s largest and most visible buyer's agency. Due to their scale and team size, Cohen Handler maintains vast relationships with selling agents across the city, generating high deal flow and frequent first-look/off-market previews. Simon Cohen is widely recognized as one of the market's most aggressive and visible dealmakers.\n  * **Best For:** Buyers who want maximum leverage, rapid execution, and sheer volume of off-market previews across multiple luxury pockets.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Established Independents & Legal-Grade Advisory\n\n* **PK Property (Peter Kelaher)**\n  * **Core Areas:** Lower North Shore (Mosman, Clifton Gardens, Neutral Bay), Northern Beaches, Eastern Suburbs.\n  * **Reputation:** Founded in 1997, PK Property is Sydney's first dedicated buyer's agency. Peter Kelaher is known for firm negotiation tactics and extensive tenure. They have completed thousands of acquisitions and are deeply entrenched in Sydney’s blue-ribbon markets, particularly on the North Shore.\n  * **Best For:** Buyers wanting a seasoned, battle-tested negotiator who knows how to dissect vendor strategies and manage aggressive auctions.\n\n* **Curtis Associates (Chris Curtis)**\n  * **Core Areas:** CBD luxury penthouses, Inner Sydney, Eastern Suburbs, Lower North Shore.\n  * **Reputation:** Headed by Chris Curtis—a former barrister and Macquarie Bank property executive—this firm offers strict, legal-grade due diligence and complete independence. Curtis Associates does not sell real estate, manage rentals, or broker finance, avoiding ancillary conflicts of interest.\n  * **Best For:** Buyers seeking meticulous contractual review, legal and planning analysis, and conflict-free representation.\n\n---\n\n### How to Choose the Right Prestige Advocate for Your Brief\n\nWhen acquiring a luxury residence in Sydney, evaluate prospective advocates against these criteria:\n\n1. **Sub-Market Specialisation:** While most top advocates will service greater Sydney, true off-market flow requires localized intimacy. For instance, the dynamics of acquiring a harborfront mansion in **Vaucluse/Point Piper** differ significantly from securing an estate in **Mosman** or a beachfront reserve in **Manly/Palm Beach**. Match your firm to the specific corridor.\n2. **True Independence:** Ensure the agency is a member of **REBAA** (Real Estate Buyers Agents Association of Australia) or operates strictly on buyer representation. They must never accept referral fees or dual representation from selling agencies or property developers.\n3. **Discretion & Privacy Protocols:** In the luxury space, buyer identity is an asset. Top advocates should offer structured anonymity—such as signing non-disclosure agreements (NDAs), acting under power-of-attorney or nominee clauses, and shielding private details from selling campaigns.\n4. **Agent Relationships:** The best prestige advocates have an established rapport with top sales agents (e.g., from Ray White Double Bay, Highland, BresicWhitney, Sotheby's, and Forbes Global Properties) where mutual trust ensures their registered buyers are notified before a campaign goes public.",
